From ddc74a030117d5b72d068d0494c0bb619282c0c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ci <sean@seandonahoe.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:10:51 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(headless): P44 -- an execution budget, not only a token
 budget, in the denial line and the guides

P44 adds the model-call and runtime limit rules (execution_model_call_limit,
execution_runtime_limit) to the shell's ExecutionBudgetRule. The pager already
decodes them through the same path (from_acp_error -> ExecutionBudget(rule), exit
3, the rule's own id and remedy on the record); this only stops the stderr line
and the unknown-rule remedy calling every budget a token budget, and lists the two
rules in the headless guide's rule table (which the_guide_lists_every_rule pins)
and in the agent guide's budget-denial table.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
